    <bpmn:process id="W_W1172" name="W1172. Tool Rental Fleet Procurement, Lifecycle Planning &amp; Retirement Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual rental fleet planning cycle; or individual unit reaches usage threshold for retirement; or new tool category demand identified
Frequency: Annual planning; quarterly procurement; ad-hoc retirement decisions
Volume: ~1,500 active rental units chain-wide; ~200–300 units replaced/added annually
Owner: Rental Fleet Manager (HQ Merchandising)
Participants: Category Manager (Tools), Procurement, Store Manager, Finance, Maintenance Supervisor
Source: workflow W1172 — Tool Rental Fleet Procurement, Lifecycle Planning &amp; Retirement Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1172_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1172_Lane1" name="Rental Fleet Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1172_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1172_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1172_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1172_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1172_Lane2" name="Procurement">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1172_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1172_Lane3" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1172_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1172_Lane4" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1172_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1172_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1172_Start6" name="Annual rental fleet planning cycle; or individual unit reaches usage threshold for…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1172_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1172_Task7" name="Annual fleet plan">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Annual fleet plan: Rental Fleet Manager compiles annual fleet plan: (a) current fleet age and condition by tool category; (b) utilization rate per unit (rental days/available days) — target ≥ 60%; (c) maintenance cost trend per unit; (d) revenue per unit vs. carrying cost; (e) customer complaint rate by unit age; (f) identify categories for expansion (new store openings, new tool types) and categories for contraction (low-demand tools); (g) budget request to Finance per W489
Responsible (R): Rental Fleet Manager
Accountable (A): Category Manager (Tools)
Duration: 2–3 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1172_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1172_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1172_Task8" name="Procurement &amp; deployment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Procurement &amp; deployment: For approved fleet additions: (a) Procurement issues RFP per W224 to tool manufacturers (Bosch, Makita, DeWalt, Hilti) for professional-grade rental fleet pricing; (b) evaluate on: durability rating, parts availability in Philippines, manufacturer rental program support, warranty terms; (c) Finance approves CAPEX per W21; (d) receive new units at DC; register in ERP as individual rental assets with serial number; (e) distribute to stores based on fleet plan allocation; (f) Store Manager assigns storage location and ensures staff training on new equipment per W139
Responsible (R): Procurement / Rental Fleet Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 4–6 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1172_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1172_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1172_Task9" name="Lifecycle tracking">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Lifecycle tracking: System tracks per-unit lifecycle metrics: (a) total rental count, (b) total operating hours, (c) maintenance events and cost, (d) revenue generated, (e) days out of service for maintenance; triggers alerts at: (i) 500 operating hours: major PM required, (ii) 1,000 hours or 3 years: retirement review, (iii) maintenance cost &gt; 40% of replacement value: mandatory retirement review
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Rental Fleet Manager
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1172_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1172_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1172_Task10" name="Retirement decision">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Retirement decision: Rental Fleet Manager reviews units flagged for retirement: (a) compare maintenance cost trend to replacement cost; (b) assess reliability risk (customer complaint rate, breakdown frequency); (c) determine disposition: (i) sell to employee at book value, (ii) sell to used equipment dealer, (iii) transfer to store demo/display inventory, (iv) scrap if beyond repair; (d) initiate replacement procurement per Step 2
Responsible (R): Rental Fleet Manager
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 30 min/unit</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1172_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1172_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1172_Task11" name="Disposition execution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Disposition execution: For retired units: (a) remove from rental inventory in ERP; (b) Finance processes asset disposal per W39 (gain/loss on disposal); (c) if sold: process through POS as used equipment sale; (d) if scrapped: document destruction for tax purposes; (e) update fleet plan with replacement unit
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Finance
Accountable (A): Rental Fleet Manager
Duration: 1–2 hours/unit</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1172_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1172_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1172_Task12" name="Quarterly fleet performance review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Quarterly fleet performance review: Rental Fleet Manager presents quarterly fleet report to Category Manager: (a) fleet utilization by category, (b) revenue per unit and ROI, (c) maintenance cost ratio, (d) customer satisfaction with rental equipment, (e) upcoming retirement schedule, (f) recommended category additions/removals
Responsible (R): Rental Fleet Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 4 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1172_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1172_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1172_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1172_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-276 (ensure controlled execution — Tool Rental &amp; Equipment (PA-12.2).) | - operational: Rental Fleet Manager (HQ Merchandising) review and approval gate
Owner: Rental Fleet Manager (HQ Merchandising)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1172_Assoc15" sourceRef="W1172_Annotation14" targetRef="W1172_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
