    <bpmn:process id="W_W1375" name="W1375. Tool Rental Overdue Return Escalation, Recovery &amp; Penalty Processing" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Rented tool not returned by scheduled return date/time; system detects overdue status
Frequency: ~150–300 overdue returns/month chain-wide (~10–20% of rentals, concentrated on weekend rentals)
Volume: ~0.75–1.5 overdue returns per store per month
Owner: CSR (initial contact); Store Manager (escalation)
Participants: CSR, Store Manager, Customer, Rental Fleet Manager (HQ), Finance (deposit forfeiture), Legal (unreturned equipment)
Source: workflow W1375 — Tool Rental Overdue Return Escalation, Recovery &amp; Penalty Processing</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1375_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1375_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1375_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1375_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1375_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1375_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1375_Lane2" name="CSR">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1375_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1375_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1375_Lane3" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1375_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1375_Lane4" name="Rental Fleet Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1375_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1375_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1375_End15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1375_Start6" name="Rented tool not returned by scheduled return date/time; system detects overdue status">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1375_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1375_Task7" name="System detects overdue status at 1 hour past scheduled return time: sends…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: System detects overdue status at 1 hour past scheduled return time: sends automated SMS/app push to customer: &quot;Your rental of [tool] was due at [time]. Please return to [store] as soon as possible. Late fees may apply per your rental agreement.&quot;
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1375_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1375_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1375_Task8" name="If not returned within 4 hours of due time: CSR calls customer: (a) confirms…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: If not returned within 4 hours of due time: CSR calls customer: (a) confirms customer received overdue notification; (b) asks for expected return time; (c) if customer needs extension: CSR processes rental extension in system — calculates additional rental days at standard rate, confirms extension does not conflict with existing reservation per W1318; (d) if extension conflicts with reservation: CSR offers alternative (return now, or swap to different tool category, or transfer reservation to another store with availability)
Responsible (R): CSR
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 5 min/call</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1375_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1375_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1375_Task9" name="If not returned by end of next business day (24+ hours overdue): Store Manager…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: If not returned by end of next business day (24+ hours overdue): Store Manager calls customer; emphasizes escalating late fees and deposit implications; documents conversation in system with expected return commitment
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1375_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1375_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1375_Task10" name="System calculates and posts late fees: (a) standard daily rental rate applied…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: System calculates and posts late fees: (a) standard daily rental rate applied for each calendar day past return date (including day of return); (b) late fees deducted from security deposit first; (c) if late fees exceed deposit amount: customer notified of additional amount due; (d) system tracks cumulative late fees and remaining deposit balance
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1375_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1375_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1375_Task11" name="If not returned within 3 days (72+ hours overdue) and customer unreachable…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: If not returned within 3 days (72+ hours overdue) and customer unreachable after 3 contact attempts: (a) system automatically flags tool as &quot;Overdue — Deposit Forfeiture&quot;; (b) full security deposit forfeited; (c) CSR sends formal demand letter via registered mail (PhilPost) and email: demands return of equipment within 5 business days or payment of replacement value; (d) customer account flagged in loyalty system — future rentals blocked until resolution
Responsible (R): System / CSR / Store Manager
Accountable (A): Rental Fleet Manager
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1375_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1375_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1375_Task12" name="If not returned within 10 days of original due date: (a) case escalated to…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: If not returned within 10 days of original due date: (a) case escalated to Rental Fleet Manager at HQ; (b) Rental Fleet Manager reviews: equipment value, customer history, contact attempts, any dispute or complaint linked to the rental; (c) if equipment value &lt; PHP 20,000: Rental Fleet Manager authorizes write-off as loss per W92; equipment removed from rental fleet; (d) if equipment value ≥ PHP 20,000: case escalated to VP Legal for formal recovery action (demand letter from legal counsel, potential small claims filing)
Responsible (R): Rental Fleet Manager / VP Legal
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 30 min/case</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1375_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1375_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1375_Task13" name="Customer returns overdue tool at any point: (a) standard W139 inbound…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Customer returns overdue tool at any point: (a) standard W139 inbound inspection performed; (b) late fees and any damage fees calculated per W139.6; (c) security deposit applied: (i) if deposit covers late fees + damage: remainder refunded; (ii) if fees exceed deposit: customer pays additional amount at POS; (d) customer loyalty flag removed if case resolved; (e) system closes overdue case
Responsible (R): CSR / Cashier / Stock Associate
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1375_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1375_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1375_Task14" name="Monthly: Rental Fleet Manager reviews overdue analytics: (a) overdue rate by…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Monthly: Rental Fleet Manager reviews overdue analytics: (a) overdue rate by store, tool category, and customer segment (trade vs. B2C); (b) average overdue duration; (c) deposit forfeiture rate; (d) equipment write-off value; (e) repeat offender rate; (f) stores with consistently high overdue rates reviewed for process improvement (better customer screening, higher deposits for high-risk categories)
Responsible (R): Rental Fleet Manager
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 2 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1375_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1375_End15" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1375_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1375_Annotation16">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-276 (ensure controlled execution — Tool Rental &amp; Equipment (PA-12.2).) | - operational: CSR (initial contact); Store Manager (escalation) review and approval gate
Owner: CSR (initial contact); Store Manager (escalation)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1375_Assoc17" sourceRef="W1375_Annotation16" targetRef="W1375_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
