    <bpmn:process id="W_W1318" name="W1318. Tool Rental Reservation, Waitlist &amp; Scheduling" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer requests advance booking for a rental tool via mobile app, phone, or in-store; or system identifies peak-demand window approaching (weekends, holiday construction periods)
Frequency: Daily; ~30–50 reservation requests chain-wide/day
Volume: ~1,000–1,500 reservations/month; peak on Friday–Saturday for weekend projects
Owner: Store Manager
Participants: Customer, CSR, Store Manager, Rental Fleet Manager (HQ), System
Source: workflow W1318 — Tool Rental Reservation, Waitlist &amp; Scheduling</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1318_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1318_Lane1" name="Customer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1318_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1318_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1318_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1318_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1318_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1318_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1318_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1318_Lane3" name="Rental Fleet Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1318_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1318_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1318_Start5" name="Customer requests advance booking for a rental tool via mobile app, phone, or in-store…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1318_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1318_Task6" name="Customer reservation request">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Customer reservation request: Customer submits reservation via: (a) BuildRight mobile app &quot;Rent Tools&quot; section — selects store, tool category, preferred date/time window, and rental duration (half-day, full-day, multi-day); (b) phone call to store CSR; (c) walk-in request at customer service counter; system checks real-time availability of requested tool category at selected store for the requested date range, considering existing reservations and currently rented units with scheduled return dates
Responsible (R): Customer / CSR / System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 3–5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1318_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1318_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1318_Task7" name="Availability confirmation &amp; booking">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Availability confirmation &amp; booking: If tool available: (a) system creates reservation record with unique reservation ID; (b) reservation held for 2 hours pending customer confirmation; (c) customer receives SMS/app confirmation with reservation ID, pickup time window, store location, and rental rate; (d) system blocks the unit from other reservations for the booked period; (e) CSR reminds customer of required ID and deposit amount per W139
Responsible (R): System / CSR
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated + 2 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1318_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1318_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1318_Task8" name="Waitlist management">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Waitlist management: If tool unavailable for requested period: (a) system offers alternatives: (i) different dates with availability, (ii) same tool at nearest store with availability (with distance and transfer feasibility), (iii) equivalent tool in same category (e.g., Bosch jackhammer if DeWalt jackhammer unavailable per W279 substitution rules); (b) if no alternatives acceptable: customer placed on waitlist with preferred date range; (c) system monitors cancellations and returns across all stores for waitlisted tool categories; (d) when availability opens: system auto-notifies waitlisted customers by SMS/app push in queue order; customer has 1 hour to confirm before system moves to next waitlisted customer
Responsible (R): System / CSR
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: Automated + 5 min per waitlist interaction</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1318_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1318_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1318_Task9" name="Cross-store reservation fulfillment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Cross-store reservation fulfillment: For high-demand categories where the local store has no availability: (a) system identifies nearest store with available unit (within 30 km or same island per W22 transfer logistics); (b) Rental Fleet Manager approves cross-store transfer for rental purposes; (c) unit transferred to requesting store per W22 with &quot;Rental Reservation&quot; priority flag; (d) system updates availability at both stores; (e) customer notified of pickup location and any slight timing adjustment
Responsible (R): Rental Fleet Manager / System
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 30 min coordination + transfer time</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1318_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1318_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1318_Task10" name="Demand-based fleet scheduling">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Demand-based fleet scheduling: Weekly: system generates rental demand forecast per store: (a) historical rental patterns by day-of-week, season, and local construction activity; (b) upcoming reservations vs. available fleet; (c) stores with consistently &gt; 80% weekend utilization flagged for fleet augmentation per W1172; (d) stores with &lt; 30% utilization flagged for potential fleet reduction or cross-store sharing; (e) Rental Fleet Manager reviews weekly demand report and adjusts inter-store unit distribution if needed
Responsible (R): System / Rental Fleet Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 1 hour/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1318_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1318_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1318_Task11" name="Reservation no-show management">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Reservation no-show management: If customer fails to pick up reserved tool within the pickup window (typically 2 hours): (a) system sends SMS/app reminder 30 minutes before window closes; (b) if no pickup by window end: reservation cancelled; unit released for walk-in or waitlist customers; (c) repeat no-show customers (3+ in 6 months) flagged in system — future reservations require deposit pre-payment via GCash/card to secure booking; (d) Store Manager may grant exceptions for documented emergencies
Responsible (R): System / Store Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1318_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1318_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1318_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1318_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-276 (ensure controlled execution — Tool Rental &amp; Equipment (PA-12.2).) | - operational: must enforce return deadlines or proactively offer alternative units
Owner: Store Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1318_Assoc14" sourceRef="W1318_Annotation13" targetRef="W1318_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1318_Flow15" sourceRef="W1318_Start5" targetRef="W1318_Task6" />
