    <bpmn:process id="W_W1319" name="W1319. Tool Rental Customer Safety Briefing, Liability Waiver &amp; Equipment Operation Acknowledgment" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer proceeds with tool rental after reservation (W1318) or walk-in (W139); required before tool release at step W139.3
Frequency: Per rental transaction; ~1,000–1,500 rentals/month chain-wide
Volume: ~50–75 safety briefings per store per month
Owner: Department Supervisor
Participants: Customer, Stock Associate (briefing conductor), Store Manager
Source: workflow W1319 — Tool Rental Customer Safety Briefing, Liability Waiver &amp; Equipment Operation Acknowledgment</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1319_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1319_Lane1" name="Stock Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1319_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1319_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1319_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1319_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1319_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1319_Lane2" name="Customer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1319_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1319_Lane3" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1319_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1319_Lane4" name="Department Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1319_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1319_End14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1319_Start6" name="Customer proceeds with tool rental after reservation (W1318) or walk-in (W139); required…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1319_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1319_Task7" name="Pre-briefing customer assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Pre-briefing customer assessment: Before conducting the safety briefing: (a) Stock Associate verifies customer is ≥ 18 years old (government-issued ID check, per W139.1); (b) visual assessment: customer appears alert, not under influence of alcohol or drugs, and physically capable of operating the equipment; (c) if customer appears impaired or is a minor: Stock Associate politely declines rental and informs Store Manager; (d) Stock Associate asks customer: &quot;Have you operated this type of equipment before?&quot; — answer recorded in system for briefing depth adjustment
Responsible (R): Stock Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 2 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1319_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1319_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1319_Task8" name="Tool-specific safety briefing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Tool-specific safety briefing: Stock Associate conducts standardized safety briefing using the tool&#x27;s Safety Briefing Card (laminated, attached to each rental unit&#x27;s storage case): (a) Personal protective equipment (PPE): required PPE for the specific tool (safety goggles for grinders, ear protection for jackhammers, gloves for all power tools, dust mask for tile cutters); PPE included with rental per W139; (b) Operating instructions: start/stop procedure, speed settings, blade/bit orientation; (c) Hazard identification: kickback risk (circular saws), electrocution risk (wet conditions with electric tools), crush risk (jackhammers), burn risk (generators — hot surfaces); (d) Safe work area: clear area of bystanders, secure workpiece, ensure ventilation for indoor gas-powered equipment; (e) Emergency shutdown: how to immediately stop the tool in an emergency; (f) Prohibited uses: modifications, removal of safety guards, use in rain for electric tools, exceeding rated load capacity; (g) briefing duration: 5 min for hand tools, 8–10 min for power tools and generators
Responsible (R): Stock Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 5–10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1319_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1319_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1319_Task9" name="Liability waiver signing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Liability waiver signing: After safety briefing: (a) Stock Associate presents the Tool Rental Liability Waiver on the store tablet: (i) customer confirms receipt of safety briefing and understanding of operating instructions; (ii) customer acknowledges inherent risks of power tool operation and assumes personal responsibility for safe use; (iii) customer agrees to indemnify BuildRight for damage caused by improper operation; (iv) customer acknowledges obligation to return tool in same condition (normal wear excepted) per W139; (v) customer authorizes deposit deduction for damage or cleaning per W139.6; (b) customer signs waiver on tablet (digital signature captured with timestamp); (c) system stores signed waiver with rental transaction record; (d) a copy of the signed waiver emailed/SMSed to customer
Responsible (R): Customer / Stock Associate / System
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 3–5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1319_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1319_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1319_Task10" name="PPE issuance confirmation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: PPE issuance confirmation: Stock Associate confirms required PPE is included with the rental: (a) system auto-generates PPE checklist based on tool category; (b) Stock Associate hands over PPE items (safety goggles, ear protection, gloves, dust mask as applicable); (c) PPE items are disposable/customer-keeps — not returned with tool; (d) PPE cost included in rental fee (estimated PHP 50–150 per rental for PPE); (e) system records PPE items issued for inventory deduction
Responsible (R): Stock Associate
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 2 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1319_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1319_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1319_Task11" name="Demonstration for first-time operators">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Demonstration for first-time operators: If customer indicated no prior experience with the tool (Step 1d): (a) Stock Associate provides hands-on demonstration in the store&#x27;s designated demo area or outdoor yard; (b) customer practices starting, operating, and stopping the tool under Stock Associate supervision; (c) Stock Associate confirms customer can safely operate the tool before proceeding to release; (d) demonstration adds 10–15 min to the rental process
Responsible (R): Stock Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 10–15 min (only for first-time operators)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1319_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1319_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1319_Task12" name="Incident reporting linkage">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Incident reporting linkage: If customer reports injury during rental period or returns tool with safety-related complaint: (a) Store Manager completes incident report per W140 (workplace safety incident); (b) system links incident to rental transaction and signed waiver; (c) Store Manager investigates: was safety briefing conducted? was waiver signed? was the tool in safe operating condition at release? (d) VP Legal reviews all rental-related injuries within 24 hours; (e) findings feed into quarterly safety briefing review (Step 7)
Responsible (R): Store Manager / VP Legal
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: Per incident</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1319_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1319_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1319_Task13" name="Quarterly safety briefing review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Quarterly safety briefing review: Department Supervisor reviews rental safety metrics quarterly: (a) briefing completion rate — target 100%; (b) PPE issuance rate — target 100%; (c) waiver signing rate — target 100%; (d) first-time operator demonstration completion rate; (e) rental-related injuries, near-misses, and customer complaints; (f) update Safety Briefing Cards if tool manufacturers issue safety advisories; (g) refresh Stock Associate training on safety briefing delivery per W51
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 2 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1319_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1319_End14" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1319_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1319_Annotation15">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-276 (ensure controlled execution — Tool Rental &amp; Equipment (PA-12.2).) | - operational: offering an annual &quot;Certified Renter&quot; program — customers who pass a one-time comprehensive safety assessment receive a Certified Renter badge in the system
Owner: Department Supervisor</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1319_Assoc16" sourceRef="W1319_Annotation15" targetRef="W1319_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1319_Flow17" sourceRef="W1319_Start6" targetRef="W1319_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1319_Flow18" sourceRef="W1319_Task7" targetRef="W1319_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1319_Flow19" sourceRef="W1319_Task8" targetRef="W1319_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1319_Flow20" sourceRef="W1319_Task9" targetRef="W1319_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1319_Flow21" sourceRef="W1319_Task10" targetRef="W1319_Task11" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1319_Flow22" sourceRef="W1319_Task11" targetRef="W1319_Task12" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1319_Flow23" sourceRef="W1319_Task12" targetRef="W1319_Task13" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1319_Flow24" sourceRef="W1319_Task13" targetRef="W1319_End14" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W1319_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W1319_plane" bpmnElement="W_W1319">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1319_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W1319_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1790" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
