    <bpmn:process id="W_W1553" name="W1553. Tool Rental Fleet Seasonal Demand Management, Cross-Store Fleet Rebalancing &amp; Capital Replacement Planning" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Quarterly rental fleet review cycle; or seasonal demand shift (rainy season → dry season); or tool reaching end-of-economic-life threshold; or sustained utilization above 85% for a tool category
Frequency: Quarterly fleet planning review; continuous demand monitoring; capital replacement decisions 1–2 times/year
Volume: ~1,500 rental units across 200 stores (~7–8 units/store avg per W139/W1172/W1374: jackhammers, tile cutters, concrete mixers, generators, pressure washers, circular saws, grinders, nail guns, compressors, welders); ~15 tool categories
Owner: Rental Fleet Manager
Participants: Rental Fleet Manager, Category Manager (Tools), VP Merchandising, CFO (Capex), Store Manager, DC Logistics Coordinator
Source: workflow W1553 — Tool Rental Fleet Seasonal Demand Management, Cross-Store Fleet Rebalancing &amp; Capital Replacement Planning</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1553_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1553_Lane1" name="Rental Fleet Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1553_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1553_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1553_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1553_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1553_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1553_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1553_End9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1553_Start3" name="Quarterly rental fleet review cycle; or seasonal demand shift (rainy season → dry…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1553_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1553_Task4" name="Quarterly utilization analysis">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Quarterly utilization analysis: Rental Fleet Manager analyzes rental utilization by tool category, store, and season: (a) utilization rate = days rented ÷ days available × 100; (b) revenue per unit per month; (c) maintenance cost per unit (trend — rising maintenance cost signals end-of-life); (d) utilization heatmap by region: which stores have chronically underutilized units (utilization &lt; 30%) vs. over-demanded (utilization &gt; 85% with frequent unavailability); (e) seasonal demand index: compare current quarter utilization vs. same quarter prior year
Responsible (R): Rental Fleet Manager
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 4 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1553_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1553_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1553_Task5" name="Cross-store fleet rebalancing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Cross-store fleet rebalancing: Based on utilization analysis: (a) identify units with utilization &lt; 25% for 2+ consecutive quarters at a store — candidate for transfer to a higher-demand store; (b) identify stores with utilization &gt; 85% and frequent customer turn-aways — need additional units; (c) coordinate inter-store transfer per W22: (i) DC Logistics arranges pickup and delivery, (ii) system updates unit location assignment, (iii) receiving store conducts condition check per W139; (d) rebalancing targets: reduce fleet-wide underutilization (utilization &lt; 25%) from current ~15% of fleet to &lt; 10%; rebalancing moves: ~50–100 units/quarter
Responsible (R): Rental Fleet Manager / DC Logistics
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 4–6 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1553_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1553_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1553_Task6" name="Capital replacement assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Capital replacement assessment: Rental Fleet Manager evaluates each unit against replacement criteria: (a) age &gt; 3 years (typical rental tool lifespan: 2–4 years depending on usage intensity); (b) cumulative maintenance cost &gt; 50% of replacement value; (c) maintenance frequency &gt; 4 repairs/year; (d) safety recall or manufacturer end-of-support notice; (e) units meeting 2+ criteria: flag for replacement in next capital cycle; (f) estimated annual replacement: ~200–300 units/year (10–15% of fleet)
Responsible (R): Rental Fleet Manager
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 2 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1553_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1553_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1553_Task7" name="New fleet acquisition planning">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: New fleet acquisition planning: Based on demand trends and utilization gaps: (a) Rental Fleet Manager proposes new unit purchases: (i) tool categories with sustained utilization &gt; 80% (need fleet expansion), (ii) new tool types requested by customers (e.g., robotic lawnmowers, heat guns, floor sanders — emerging demand), (iii) stores with growing population but inadequate fleet size; (b) CFO evaluates capex request per W21: (i) ROI calculation: rental revenue per unit ÷ purchase cost, (ii) payback period target: &lt; 18 months; (c) annual new fleet acquisition budget: ~PHP 8–15M/year (~200–300 units × PHP 40–50K avg)
Responsible (R): Rental Fleet Manager / CFO
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 4 hours/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1553_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1553_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1553_Task8" name="Seasonal pre-positioning">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Seasonal pre-positioning: Before peak seasons: (a) dry season (Nov–Dec preparation): pre-position jackhammers, concrete mixers, tile cutters at stores in construction-heavy regions (Metro Manila, CALABARZON, Cebu); (b) typhoon season (May–Jun preparation): pre-position generators at stores in typhoon-prone areas (Eastern Visayas, Bicol, Northern Luzon); (c) holiday season (Oct–Nov preparation): increase inventory of popular gift-quality tools (power drills, impact drivers) for both rental and retail
Responsible (R): Rental Fleet Manager / DC Logistics
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 4 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1553_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1553_End9" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1553_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1553_Annotation10">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-276 (ensure controlled execution — Tool Rental &amp; Equipment (PA-12.2).) | - operational: standard operating procedures; system-enforced validation rules
Owner: Rental Fleet Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1553_Assoc11" sourceRef="W1553_Annotation10" targetRef="W1553_Start3" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1553_Flow12" sourceRef="W1553_Start3" targetRef="W1553_Task4" />
