    <bpmn:process id="W_W1554" name="W1554. Power Tool Rental Preventive Maintenance, Wear Parts Replacement &amp; Servicing Vendor Coordination" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Scheduled — based on rental hours counter or calendar interval per manufacturer; or post-rental customer-reported performance issue; or quarterly maintenance cycle
Frequency: Monthly scheduled PM for high-use tools (jackhammers, generators); quarterly PM for medium-use tools (tile cutters, mixers); semi-annual for low-use tools; ~330–670 PM events/month chain-wide (per the ~4,000–8,000/year Volume)
Volume: ~2,000 rental units; each unit serviced 2–6 times/year; ~4,000–8,000 PM events/year total
Owner: Rental Fleet Manager
Participants: Rental Fleet Manager, Stock Associate (store-level PM), Authorized Service Center (vendor), Department Supervisor
Source: workflow W1554 — Power Tool Rental Preventive Maintenance, Wear Parts Replacement &amp; Servicing Vendor Coordination</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1554_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1554_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1554_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1554_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1554_Lane2" name="Stock Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1554_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1554_Lane3" name="Rental Fleet Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1554_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1554_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1554_Lane4" name="Department Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1554_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1554_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1554_Start6" name="Scheduled — based on rental hours counter or calendar interval per manufacturer; or…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1554_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1554_Task7" name="PM scheduling">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: PM scheduling: Rental Fleet Manager maintains PM schedule per tool category based on manufacturer recommendations and rental usage intensity: (a) heavy-use tools (jackhammers, generators): PM every 100 rental hours or monthly, whichever comes first; (b) medium-use tools (tile cutters, concrete mixers, pressure washers): PM every 200 rental hours or quarterly; (c) light-use tools (drills, circular saws, grinders): PM every 300 rental hours or semi-annually; (d) system auto-generates PM work orders based on rental hour counters (tracked via rental transaction records)
Responsible (R): System / Rental Fleet Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated scheduling + 2 hours/month review</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1554_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1554_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1554_Task8" name="Store-level basic PM">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Store-level basic PM: Stock Associate performs basic PM tasks between rentals: (a) visual inspection: check power cord integrity, switch function, guard presence, housing cracks; (b) clean: remove concrete dust, paint splatter, debris from air vents and moving parts; (c) lubricate moving parts per manufacturer guidelines; (d) check and replace minor wear parts: carbon brushes (for universal motors), air filters (generators), cutting blades (if dull — charge to previous renter per W139 if applicable); (e) log PM completion in system with date, hours counter reading, and any findings
Responsible (R): Stock Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 15–30 min/unit</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1554_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1554_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1554_Task9" name="Authorized service center major PM">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Authorized service center major PM: For major servicing (annual overhaul, motor bearing replacement, gearbox service): (a) Rental Fleet Manager coordinates with authorized service centers per tool brand (Bosch, Makita, DeWalt have Philippine service networks): (i) schedule pickup of tools due for major PM from each store, (ii) service center performs manufacturer-specified major PM: motor testing, bearing replacement, seal replacement, calibration, safety interlock testing; (b) turnaround time: 3–5 business days per unit; (c) Rental Fleet Manager tracks tools at service center — system flags units out for &gt; 7 days for follow-up; (d) store temporarily reassigns rental availability: remove serviced units from reservation system per W1318
Responsible (R): Rental Fleet Manager / Service Center
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: Coordination: 2–3 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1554_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1554_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1554_Task10" name="Wear part inventory management">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Wear part inventory management: Department Supervisor tracks replacement wear parts at store level: (a) common consumables kept in-stock per store: carbon brushes, air filters, blades, belts, safety guards, power cords; (b) reorder point per part based on replacement frequency: auto-generate PO per W2 for replenishment from vendor; (c) wear part cost tracking per unit: if cumulative wear part cost exceeds 40% of unit replacement cost, flag for capital replacement evaluation per W1553
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): Rental Fleet Manager
Duration: 1 hour/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1554_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1554_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1554_Task11" name="PM compliance monitoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: PM compliance monitoring: Rental Fleet Manager monitors PM compliance across 200 stores: (a) PM completion rate: % of scheduled PMs completed on time (target: ≥ 95%); (b) overdue PM alerts: units with overdue PM &gt; 7 days — system blocks unit from rental availability until PM completed; (c) PM cost per unit by tool category — identify categories with abnormally high PM costs for potential fleet replacement; (d) quarterly PM compliance report to Category Manager and VP Merchandising
Responsible (R): Rental Fleet Manager
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 2 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1554_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1554_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1554_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1554_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-276 (ensure controlled execution — Tool Rental &amp; Equipment (PA-12.2).) | - operational: system-block for units with overdue PM
Owner: Rental Fleet Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1554_Assoc14" sourceRef="W1554_Annotation13" targetRef="W1554_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1554_Flow15" sourceRef="W1554_Start6" targetRef="W1554_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1554_Flow16" sourceRef="W1554_Task7" targetRef="W1554_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1554_Flow17" sourceRef="W1554_Task8" targetRef="W1554_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1554_Flow18" sourceRef="W1554_Task9" targetRef="W1554_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1554_Flow19" sourceRef="W1554_Task10" targetRef="W1554_Task11" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1554_Flow20" sourceRef="W1554_Task11" targetRef="W1554_End12" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W1554_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W1554_plane" bpmnElement="W_W1554">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1554_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W1554_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1370" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1554_Lane2_di" bpmnElement="W1554_Lane2" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="250" width="1370" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1554_Lane3_di" bpmnElement="W1554_Lane3" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="420" width="1370" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1554_Lane4_di" bpmnElement="W1554_Lane4" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="590" width="1370" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1554_Task7_di" bpmnElement="W1554_Task7"><dc:Bounds x="400" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1554_Task8_di" bpmnElement="W1554_Task8"><dc:Bounds x="610" y="295" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1554_Task9_di" bpmnElement="W1554_Task9"><dc:Bounds x="820" y="465" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1554_Task10_di" bpmnElement="W1554_Task10"><dc:Bounds x="1030" y="635" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1554_Task11_di" bpmnElement="W1554_Task11"><dc:Bounds x="1240" y="465" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1554_Start6_di" bpmnElement="W1554_Start6"><dc:Bounds x="290" y="147" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1554_End12_di" bpmnElement="W1554_End12"><dc:Bounds x="1470" y="657" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1554_Annotation13_di" bpmnElement="W1554_Annotation13"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="800" width="360" height="60" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1554_Flow15_di" bpmnElement="W1554_Flow15"><di:waypoint x="326" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="400" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1554_Flow16_di" bpmnElement="W1554_Flow16"><di:waypoint x="580" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="610" y="335" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1554_Flow17_di" bpmnElement="W1554_Flow17"><di:waypoint x="790" y="335" /><di:waypoint x="820" y="505" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1554_Flow18_di" bpmnElement="W1554_Flow18"><di:waypoint x="1000" y="505" /><di:waypoint x="1030" y="675" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1554_Flow19_di" bpmnElement="W1554_Flow19"><di:waypoint x="1210" y="675" /><di:waypoint x="1240" y="505" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1554_Flow20_di" bpmnElement="W1554_Flow20"><di:waypoint x="1420" y="505" /><di:waypoint x="1470" y="675" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1554_Assoc14_di" bpmnElement="W1554_Assoc14"><di:waypoint x="340" y="800" /><di:waypoint x="308" y="183" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      </bpmndi:BPMNPlane>
    </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
    <bpmn:process id="W_W1555" name="W1555. Tool Rental Customer Damage Assessment, Repair Cost Recovery &amp; Dispute Resolution" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer returns rental tool with visible damage beyond normal wear; or tool malfunction reported during rental period; or missing accessories/components at return
Frequency: ~150–250 damage incidents/month chain-wide (~10–15% of rental returns have some damage beyond normal wear)
Volume: ~1,000–1,500 rentals/month; ~150–250 with damage assessment needed; ~30–50 with chargeable damage; ~5–10 with customer disputes
Owner: Department Supervisor
Participants: Department Supervisor, Stock Associate, Store Manager, Customer, Rental Fleet Manager, Customer Service Rep
Source: workflow W1555 — Tool Rental Customer Damage Assessment, Repair Cost Recovery &amp; Dispute Resolution</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1555_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1555_Lane1" name="Stock Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1555_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1555_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1555_Lane2" name="Department Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1555_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1555_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1555_Lane3" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1555_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1555_Lane4" name="Rental Fleet Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1555_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1555_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1555_Start6" name="Customer returns rental tool with visible damage beyond normal wear; or tool malfunction…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1555_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1555_Task7" name="Return inspection">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Return inspection: Upon tool return per W139: (a) Stock Associate conducts standardized return checklist: (i) compare tool condition against pre-rental condition photos (taken at W139.3 checkout — 4 photos: front, back, left side, right side plus close-ups of any pre-existing damage), (ii) power test: plug in and run for 30 seconds — check for unusual noise, vibration, sparking, or overheating, (iii) accessory check: all included accessories present (blades, bits, hoses, guards, carrying case), (iv) cleanliness: tool returned in reasonable condition (excessive concrete/mud/paint requires cleaning fee); (b) classify damage: (i) Normal Wear — minor scratches, paint chips, faded labels; no charge, (ii) Chargeable Damage — broken handle, cracked housing, burnt smell (motor overload), missing guard, water damage; proceed to Step 2, (iii) Total Loss — tool destroyed, stolen, or unrepairable; proceed to Step 3
Responsible (R): Stock Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 5–10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1555_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1555_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1555_Task8" name="Damage assessment &amp; cost estimate">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Damage assessment &amp; cost estimate: For chargeable damage: (a) Department Supervisor assesses repair scope: (i) parts needed (reference manufacturer parts list), (ii) labor estimate (internal repair if minor, authorized service center if major per W1554), (iii) total repair cost estimate; (b) compare repair cost vs. tool replacement value: (i) if repair cost &lt; 50% of replacement: charge repair cost, (ii) if repair cost &gt; 50% of replacement: charge replacement value (total loss); (c) system generates damage assessment report with photos, cost estimate, and customer charge
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): Rental Fleet Manager
Duration: 15–20 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1555_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1555_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1555_Task9" name="Customer notification &amp; charge">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Customer notification &amp; charge: (a) Department Supervisor informs customer of damage finding and estimated charge: (i) show pre-rental vs. return photos for comparison, (ii) explain damage classification (normal wear vs. chargeable), (iii) present cost estimate; (b) if customer accepts: deduct from deposit held per W139; if damage exceeds deposit: customer pays difference at POS; (c) if customer disputes: proceed to Step 4
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor / Customer
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 10–15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1555_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1555_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1555_Task10" name="Dispute resolution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Dispute resolution: If customer disputes damage charge: (a) Level 1 (Store Manager): Store Manager reviews photos, damage assessment, and rental history; mediates between Department Supervisor and customer; may offer compromise (split cost 50/50 as goodwill for loyal trade customers); (b) Level 2 (Rental Fleet Manager): if unresolved at store level, Rental Fleet Manager reviews case remotely — examines pre-rental photos, maintenance history per W1554 (was tool already in declining condition?), and customer rental history (first-time damage or repeat offender?); (c) Level 3 (COO): for high-value disputes (&gt; PHP 10,000) or threats of legal action; COO makes final decision — may waive charge to preserve major trade account relationship; (d) all dispute resolutions documented in system for pattern analysis
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Rental Fleet Manager / COO
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 15–30 min per dispute</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1555_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1555_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1555_Task11" name="Pattern analysis &amp; chronic offender management">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Pattern analysis &amp; chronic offender management: Monthly: (a) Rental Fleet Manager analyzes damage incident data: (i) damage rate by tool category (which tools get damaged most?), (ii) damage rate by store (do some stores have higher damage rates — indicating lax pre-rental inspection?), (iii) repeat damage offenders (customers with 2+ damage incidents in 12 months); (b) for repeat offenders: (i) first incident: standard charge, (ii) second incident: standard charge + mandatory demonstration per W1319 Step 5 regardless of experience, (iii) third incident: increased deposit (double standard) or rental privileges suspended for 6 months; (c) findings feed into W1553 fleet planning (tools with chronic damage may indicate quality issues requiring fleet replacement)
Responsible (R): Rental Fleet Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 2 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1555_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1555_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1555_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1555_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-276 (ensure controlled execution — Tool Rental &amp; Equipment (PA-12.2).) | - operational: Department Supervisor review and approval gate
Owner: Department Supervisor</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
